# Keep the serverless bundle small. Vercel's Python functions have a hard
# uncompressed size limit and the ML dependencies already consume most of it,
# so nothing that isn't needed to SERVE a request should ship.
#
# The deployed app loads exactly these repo files at import time (verified):
#   backend/main.py, backend/model_service.py, backend/schemas.py,
#   score_upload.py, scoring.py, model_adapter.py, explanation_layer.py,
#   patient_options.py, train_adherence_model.py  (imported for its column
#   policy constants -- excluding it breaks the import chain), plus model.pkl
#   and docs/ for the front end. None of those may be listed below.

# Training / evaluation / batch scripts - not imported by the app.
evaluate_model.py
run_explanations.py
predict.py
test_*.py
HANDOFF.txt

# Datasets and batch artifacts. The live API scores uploaded or form-built
# patients; it never reads these files.
Synthetic Patients Processed.csv
synthetic_patients_new_500.csv
test_upload_sample.csv
patients_scored.json
patients_high_risk.json
test_results.json
input/
output/

# Local env / tooling / secrets
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.github/
.claude/
backend/.env
